<mxCell id="n22" value="FINDING G1 (High, VERIFIED). manual_add_booking sends a NAIVE datetime. (a) It is stored into a timestamptz column via the server&#x27;s local tz — a 10:00 walk-in came back as 07:30 IST on this box; on a UTC server it would read 15:30. Every manual service booking shows the wrong time on My Day and the slip. (b) has_calendar_conflict then compares naive vs tz-aware and raises TypeError → 500 on the 2nd overlapping booking. The existing test hides this by reusing one session; a fresh session reproduces the crash." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;align=left;verticalAlign=top;size=14;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="520" y="630" width="360" height="220" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="e23" value="" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=block;dashed=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#b85450;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="n11" target="n22"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="n24" value="FINDING G2 (Med). The Add form hardcodes every name as section=&#x27;pair&#x27;, status=&#x27;living&#x27;, and service purpose as &#x27;khushali_nu&#x27;. A manually-added Patet machi records its DEPARTED pair as &#x27;living&#x27;; farmayeshne and real purpose are never captured. Doc 07 says closed-vocab fields (purpose) must be selectable — here purpose isn&#x27;t even offered." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;align=left;verticalAlign=top;size=14;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="120" y="630" width="340" height="180" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="e25" value="" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=block;dashed=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#b85450;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=1;entryY=0;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="n10" target="n24"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="n26" value="Multi-agyari: My Day merges all agyaries (good); Machi Board is per-agyari via the switcher. But the switcher only lists ALREADY-joined agyaries — no &#x27;join another&#x27; action (see Finding D1, Flow 2)." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;align=left;verticalAlign=top;size=14;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="980" y="320" width="300" height="110" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="e27" value="" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=block;dashed=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#d6b656;exitX=1;exitY=0.3;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.3;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="n2" target="n26"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
